                        <field name="dc_description">Water consumption of steam locomotives was considerable. The tenders of the express train machines covered up to 38 m ³ of water, but this quantity was only sufficient for a driving range of 300 km. On many subway stations and on the railway works water cranes were standing by the track for this purpose. This model shows a typical design of the Prussian railways around 1890. On the railway premises of the Deutsches Technikmuseum such a crane is preserved in the original.<br/>
<br/>
Traffic and construction museum. Official guide through the collections/Transport and Construction Museum Berlin. Berlin: Elsner, 1943. P. 61 (Deutsches Technikmuseum) </field>
